#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The ask-ollama helper: a model bridge to an Ollama server.

It is one file that imports the standard library and the workbench kit (``wbkit``); the launcher runs a
private copy of it through the kit runner with nothing beside it.

    ask-ollama ask [--model <name>] [--context <tokens>] [--effort <level> | --thinking on|off] [--max-output <tokens>]
                   [--temperature <value>] [--keep-alive <value>] [--timeout <seconds>] [--root <path>] [--schema <path>]
                   [--server <name>] [--confine]                       the prompt is on standard input
    ask-ollama check                                                   read-only: the endpoint file, no connection
    ask-ollama models [--server <name>] [--timeout <seconds>]          read-only: the configured models the server has
    ask-ollama embed [--model <name>] [--context <tokens>] [--keep-alive <value>] [--server <name>] [--timeout <seconds>]
                     [--confine]
                                              one JSON object ``{"texts": [...]}`` on standard input; vectors out

The contract is ``docs/specs/model-bridge.md`` (version 2) and the behaviour is ``docs/specs/ask-ollama.md``. The
server is a named record of ``bridge-endpoints.json`` in the guarded store (decisions ``2026-11-01-endpoint-records-in-the-store`` and
``2026-11-02-model-configurations-in-endpoint-records``, and for the temperature and the keep_alive
``2026-11-02-temperature-and-keep-alive-in-model-sections``), never an address in an argument, an environment variable or a tracked
file. A record holds a section for each model a call may use: only a configured model is used, and its section gives the window and, when it holds them, the defaults of a call (an effort or a
switch for thinking, an output limit, a temperature and how long the server keeps the model loaded), which a call argument
replaces. A prompt that is probably larger than the window (its
size in bytes above the window times the section's bytes per token) is not sent. The helper makes one request, to the host and
port of that record and to no other, follows no redirect, verifies an ``https`` server, keeps no state, writes nothing and
logs nothing. What the server returns is data: it is classified and copied, never run and never believed.
"""

